{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For. Orion.</b> Some say that כסיל is the star that is near the southern foundation, whose appearance causes camels to die, and in my opinion it is the heart of Scorpio. It is possible that כסילים is from the derivation of כסלים (Leviticus 3:4), for they are near the foundations. And Rabbi Yonah says that כסיל is one, and other stars are joined to it like it, as in בתי השן (Amos 3:15):" "<b>Shall grow dim.</b> Like יחלו (Judges 20:31), from doubled [root] verbs, and here it is a passive verb. And so too בהלו נרו (Job 29:3), likewise יגיה; and the proof is יגיה חשכי (Psalms 18:29):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The phrase 'whose appearance causes camels to die' is hyper-literal; the reference is to a medieval belief about the star Canopus, but no interpretation is added."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:37.805687481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}